"use strict";
module.exports = /*#__PURE__*/JSON.parse('{"pluralForm":"nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);","translations":{"A course can apply filters to a pool without changing the original pool. Typical filters are exam key, chapter key or a fixed list of question IDs. That is why a course pool can show fewer questions than the raw pool total.":"A course can apply filters to a pool without changing the original pool. Typical filters are exam key, chapter key or a fixed list of question IDs. That is why a course pool can show fewer questions than the raw pool total.","A course is the learning space for one class or exam track. A pool is a set of questions. Courses can contain several pools, and the same pool can be reused in different contexts without rewriting the questions.":"A course is the learning space for one class or exam track. A pool is a set of questions. Courses can contain several pools, and the same pool can be reused in different contexts without rewriting the questions.","A due card is ready for review again based on its current box and schedule. If no cards are due, the dashboard shows that you are caught up for now.":"A due card is ready for review again based on its current box and schedule. If no cards are due, the dashboard shows that you are caught up for now.","A duel puts you head-to-head against another learner.":"A duel puts you head-to-head against another learner.","A duel starts either by creating a new duel and sharing the code, or by joining an existing duel with that code. Both players then enter the lobby and have to mark themselves ready before the first question begins.":"A duel starts either by creating a new duel and sharing the code, or by joining an existing duel with that code. Both players then enter the lobby and have to mark themselves ready before the first question begins.","A pool is locked when the course has at least one required and enforced pool that you have not completed yet. In that case, optional pools stay unavailable until every filtered question in the required pool was answered at least once.":"A pool is locked when the course has at least one required and enforced pool that you have not completed yet. In that case, optional pools stay unavailable until every filtered question in the required pool was answered at least once.","A streak tracks how many days in a row you stayed active. Milestones can trigger extra celebration feedback, but the core value is that it helps you stay consistent over time.":"A streak tracks how many days in a row you stayed active. Milestones can trigger extra celebration feedback, but the core value is that it helps you stay consistent over time.","Admin Settings":"Admin Settings","After each answer you see whether it was correct, which answer was right, and when available also an explanation or instructor note. That makes Training the fastest mode for learning from mistakes immediately.":"After each answer you see whether it was correct, which answer was right, and when available also an explanation or instructor note. That makes Training the fastest mode for learning from mistakes immediately.","After the final score, you see the winner and can start a rematch. If a duel was league-linked, the result is also written back into the league standings.":"After the final score, you see the winner and can start a rematch. If a duel was league-linked, the result is also written back into the league standings.","After the regular season, the top four move into the Champions League bracket. Those matches use the dedicated CL pool and the longer question count defined for the final round.":"After the regular season, the top four move into the Champions League bracket. Those matches use the dedicated CL pool and the longer question count defined for the final round.","After you answer, your choice stays visible and the question waits until the opponent also finishes that round. Then both players get the short feedback screen before the next question starts.":"After you answer, your choice stays visible and the question waits until the opponent also finishes that round. Then both players get the short feedback screen before the next question starts.","All topics":"All topics","Allow course-based instructor fallback":"Allow course-based instructor fallback","Answer":"Answer","Ask about this":"Ask about this","At the end you see your score, the number of correct answers, XP gained, streak effects and possible badge unlocks. Training may also compare your result with your average and mark a personal best.":"At the end you see your score, the number of correct answers, XP gained, streak effects and possible badge unlocks. Training may also compare your result with your average and mark a personal best.","Back":"Back","Badges unlock when you meet certain learning conditions. You can earn them through activity, consistency or mastery-related progress, and the UI shows both unlocked badges and progress toward future ones.":"Badges unlock when you meet certain learning conditions. You can earn them through activity, consistency or mastery-related progress, and the UI shows both unlocked badges and progress toward future ones.","Browse all topics":"Browse all topics","Calendar Sync gives you an ICS URL that can be subscribed to in calendar apps. It is meant to surface due cards or study reminders outside the app. Regenerating the token invalidates the old URL.":"Calendar Sync gives you an ICS URL that can be subscribed to in calendar apps. It is meant to surface due cards or study reminders outside the app. Regenerating the token invalidates the old URL.","Can I turn VirtuProf off?":"Can I turn VirtuProf off?","Challenges, standings, season flow and Champions League.":"Challenges, standings, season flow and Champions League.","Choose a course to open its learning modes, leaderboard, league and duels. Each course can have its own assigned pools and rules.":"Choose a course to open its learning modes, leaderboard, league and duels. Each course can have its own assigned pools and rules.","Choose a topic first. Then I will show the most common questions inside it.":"Choose a topic first. Then I will show the most common questions inside it.","Close":"Close","Congratulations! You unlocked a new badge: {badgeName}":"Congratulations! You unlocked a new badge: {badgeName}","Content Language changes the language used for question and answer content when translations are available. It does not change the general app interface language by itself.":"Content Language changes the language used for question and answer content when translations are available. It does not change the general app interface language by itself.","Content language, assistant toggle, calendar sync and preferences.":"Content language, assistant toggle, calendar sync and preferences.","Core basics about courses, pools, locks and language settings.":"Core basics about courses, pools, locks and language settings.","Correct answers are what matter first. If both players answer a question correctly, speed can decide the better outcome. After each question the score bar updates, so you can see the duel swing live.":"Correct answers are what matter first. If both players answer a question correctly, speed can decide the better outcome. After each question the score bar updates, so you can see the duel swing live.","Course":"Course","Courses":"Courses","Create, join and understand direct head-to-head matches.":"Create, join and understand direct head-to-head matches.","Current answer":"Current answer","Daily Challenge enabled":"Daily Challenge enabled","Daily Challenge, notifications and related toggles control how much extra guidance or reminder behavior you get. They do not rewrite your actual question data, but they can change how the app nudges and informs you.":"Daily Challenge, notifications and related toggles control how much extra guidance or reminder behavior you get. They do not rewrite your actual question data, but they can change how the app nudges and informs you.","Default language":"Default language","Describe your question or problem...":"Describe your question or problem...","Duel":"Duel","Duell":"Duell","End Exam finishes the current attempt and saves the result based on what you answered so far. Abort discards the attempt instead, so no regular result is kept.":"End Exam finishes the current attempt and saves the result based on what you answered so far. Abort discards the attempt instead, so no regular result is kept.","English":"English","Event":"Event","Exam":"Exam","Exam attempts per 24h (per pool/user)":"Exam attempts per 24h (per pool/user)","Exam cooldown (minutes)":"Exam cooldown (minutes)","Exam in {course}":"Exam in {course}","Exam mode behaves like a test run: you choose a time limit and question count, complete one continuous session, and do not get immediate correctness feedback while answering. The detailed review comes only after the exam ends.":"Exam mode behaves like a test run: you choose a time limit and question count, complete one continuous session, and do not get immediate correctness feedback while answering. The detailed review comes only after the exam ends.","Exam mode runs like a real exam: one session, no immediate feedback, full review at the end.":"Exam mode runs like a real exam: one session, no immediate feedback, full review at the end.","Exam: {pool}":"Exam: {pool}","FAQs":"FAQs","Failed to load settings":"Failed to load settings","Failed to load support tickets":"Failed to load support tickets","Failed to save settings":"Failed to save settings","Failed to save support ticket answer":"Failed to save support ticket answer","Failed to send support ticket":"Failed to send support ticket","Fast and correct answers matter: both right means speed decides the higher score bonus.":"Fast and correct answers matter: both right means speed decides the higher score bonus.","Gamification enabled":"Gamification enabled","German (Deutsch)":"German (Deutsch)","Getting Started":"Getting Started","Here you can accept or start direct duels. Once the duel starts, every answer counts and speed can break ties.":"Here you can accept or start direct duels. Once the duel starts, every answer counts and speed can break ties.","How are league standings calculated?":"How are league standings calculated?","How do I start learning in a course?":"How do I start learning in a course?","How do XP and levels work?":"How do XP and levels work?","How do badges work?":"How do badges work?","How do duels start?":"How do duels start?","How do league challenges work?":"How do league challenges work?","How does the Leitner system work?":"How does the Leitner system work?","How does the league work?":"How does the league work?","How is duel scoring decided?":"How is duel scoring decided?","I give short tips right where they help most. You can turn me off any time in Personal Settings.":"I give short tips right where they help most. You can turn me off any time in Personal Settings.","I stay in the corner now. Open me any time for short explanations or quick FAQs.":"I stay in the corner now. Open me any time for short explanations or quick FAQs.","If Content Language is set in Personal Settings, Learning tries to show translated question and answer texts in that language. If no translation exists, the original content is used.":"If Content Language is set in Personal Settings, Learning tries to show translated question and answer texts in that language. If no translation exists, the original content is used.","If disabled (recommended), only members of the configured instructor group get global instructor privileges.":"If disabled (recommended), only members of the configured instructor group get global instructor privileges.","If the explain feature is available for your app setup, Training can request a short explanation for the current question after you answered it. This is meant as extra support, not as the authoritative source over the actual solution and instructor notes.":"If the explain feature is available for your app setup, Training can request a short explanation for the current question after you answered it. This is meant as extra support, not as the authoritative source over the actual solution and instructor notes.","If the time limit expires, the exam is auto-submitted by the server. You are then taken to the results and detailed review instead of continuing the question phase.":"If the time limit expires, the exam is auto-submitted by the server. You are then taken to the results and detailed review instead of continuing the question phase.","Immediate feedback, question types and the quickest way to practice.":"Immediate feedback, question types and the quickest way to practice.","Leaderboard":"Leaderboard","League logic can resolve unfinished or expired challenge situations through forfeit handling. That prevents the season from being blocked forever and lets the standings close cleanly.":"League logic can resolve unfinished or expired challenge situations through forfeit handling. That prevents the season from being blocked forever and lets the standings close cleanly.","League play happens inside one course. Everyone plays everyone, and the top 4 move on to the final round.":"League play happens inside one course. Everyone plays everyone, and the top 4 move on to the final round.","Learning protects active exams from being answered in multiple tabs at the same time. If the exam is already active elsewhere, another tab can only show the state in read-only mode.":"Learning protects active exams from being answered in multiple tabs at the same time. If the exam is already active elsewhere, another tab can only show the state in read-only mode.","Learning sessions can award XP. As XP grows, your level increases and your progress bar moves toward the next threshold. This gives you a long-term sense of momentum across sessions.":"Learning sessions can award XP. As XP grows, your level increases and your progress bar moves toward the next threshold. This gives you a long-term sense of momentum across sessions.","Leitner":"Leitner","Leitner & Queue":"Leitner & Queue","Leitner in {course}":"Leitner in {course}","Leitner uses spaced repetition with 5 boxes. Correct answers move a card into a higher box, wrong answers send it back. Higher boxes come back less often, so the system focuses your time on weak material.":"Leitner uses spaced repetition with 5 boxes. Correct answers move a card into a higher box, wrong answers send it back. Higher boxes come back less often, so the system focuses your time on weak material.","Leitner: {pool}":"Leitner: {pool}","Liga":"Liga","Loading...":"Loading...","Mastery, leaderboard, XP, streaks and badges.":"Mastery, leaderboard, XP, streaks and badges.","Max import file size (MB)":"Max import file size (MB)","Message":"Message","More in this topic":"More in this topic","My Progress":"My Progress","My Progress focuses on your own status inside the course. It helps you see what you already mastered, how many questions you answered and where you still have weak areas.":"My Progress focuses on your own status inside the course. It helps you see what you already mastered, how many questions you answered and where you still have weak areas.","My requests":"My requests","My support tickets":"My support tickets","New ticket":"New ticket","Next":"Next","No audit events yet.":"No audit events yet.","No context available":"No context available","No support tickets yet.":"No support tickets yet.","Ok, got it":"Ok, got it","Open Duel appears once a challenge has been accepted and a duel code already exists. At that point the match is ready to be played from inside the league tab itself.":"Open Duel appears once a challenge has been accepted and a duel code already exists. At that point the match is ready to be played from inside the league tab itself.","Open a course, choose a learning mode like Training or Leitner and then pick one of the assigned pools. The mode starts only after the pool selection, so the teacher controls the available material through course pools and optional filters.":"Open a course, choose a learning mode like Training or Leitner and then pick one of the assigned pools. The mode starts only after the pool selection, so the teacher controls the available material through course pools and optional filters.","Open tickets wait for an admin reply. Answered tickets keep the latest response here.":"Open tickets wait for an admin reply. Answered tickets keep the latest response here.","Pick a pool for fast true-or-false practice. This mode is good for quick repetition and recognition.":"Pick a pool for fast true-or-false practice. This mode is good for quick repetition and recognition.","Pick a pool to review cards with spaced repetition. The system will show difficult cards more often and mastered cards less often.":"Pick a pool to review cards with spaced repetition. The system will show difficult cards more often and mastered cards less often.","Pick a pool to simulate an exam. You will finish the whole session first and only then see the full review.":"Pick a pool to simulate an exam. You will finish the whole session first and only then see the full review.","Pick a pool to start Training. You will get direct feedback after each answer, and required enforced pools may lock the optional ones until you finish them once.":"Pick a pool to start Training. You will get direct feedback after each answer, and required enforced pools may lock the optional ones until you finish them once.","Pool":"Pool","Progress & Rewards":"Progress & Rewards","Question":"Question","Question language":"Question language","Recent Audit Events":"Recent Audit Events","Refresh":"Refresh","Save":"Save","Save answer":"Save answer","Saving...":"Saving...","Send a question":"Send a question","Send ticket":"Send ticket","Sending...":"Sending...","Session":"Session","Settings & Language":"Settings & Language","Settings saved":"Settings saved","Short summary":"Short summary","Smart Queue combines due Leitner questions across pools and sorts them by priority, with the most urgent items first. It is useful when you want one focused review list instead of opening pools one by one.":"Smart Queue combines due Leitner questions across pools and sorts them by priority, with the most urgent items first. It is useful when you want one focused review list instead of opening pools one by one.","Spaced repetition, boxes, due cards and remediation.":"Spaced repetition, boxes, due cards and remediation.","Start Here":"Start Here","Subject":"Subject","Support ticket answer saved":"Support ticket answer saved","Support ticket sent":"Support ticket sent","Support tickets":"Support tickets","That one was rough. Tip: review your weakest questions in Leitner Box 1 first and then try the exam again.":"That one was rough. Tip: review your weakest questions in Leitner Box 1 first and then try the exam again.","The Leitner system sorts questions into 5 boxes based on your learning progress. Correct answers move up, wrong answers go back to Box 1.":"The Leitner system sorts questions into 5 boxes based on your learning progress. Correct answers move up, wrong answers go back to Box 1.","The higher the box, the less often you review that card. That keeps practice focused and efficient.":"The higher the box, the less often you review that card. That keeps practice focused and efficient.","The leaderboard compares learners in the same course. Depending on the view, it can show rank, XP, mastery and other activity indicators so you can see who is currently most active or strongest.":"The leaderboard compares learners in the same course. Depending on the view, it can show rank, XP, mastery and other activity indicators so you can see who is currently most active or strongest.","The leaderboard compares learners in the same course. XP, mastery and other activity indicators show who is currently ahead.":"The leaderboard compares learners in the same course. XP, mastery and other activity indicators show who is currently ahead.","The league exists inside one course. Learners challenge each other, complete linked duels and earn points in a standings table. The season also has a separate Champions League pool for the final round.":"The league exists inside one course. Learners challenge each other, complete linked duels and earn points in a standings table. The season also has a separate Champions League pool for the final round.","The league is course-specific. Challenge classmates, collect points and watch the standings change after each finished duel.":"The league is course-specific. Challenge classmates, collect points and watch the standings change after each finished duel.","The player who creates the duel chooses the pool and the number of questions. The opponent joins that exact setup through the duel code.":"The player who creates the duel chooses the pool and the number of questions. The opponent joins that exact setup through the duel code.","The review shows your score, correct and wrong counts, time taken, questions per minute and a question-by-question breakdown. Depending on the question type, you can also see your own answer, the correct answer and instructor notes.":"The review shows your score, correct and wrong counts, time taken, questions per minute and a question-by-question breakdown. Depending on the question type, you can also see your own answer, the correct answer and instructor notes.","The table tracks played matches, wins, losses, points and point difference. Points decide the ranking first, and point difference serves as the tie-breaker.":"The table tracks played matches, wins, losses, points and point difference. Points decide the ranking first, and point difference serves as the tie-breaker.","These settings apply to all users of Learning.":"These settings apply to all users of Learning.","This area":"This area","This area shows your own progress in the course, including mastery and answered questions. Use it to see where you still have gaps.":"This area shows your own progress in the course, including mastery and answered questions. Use it to see where you still have gaps.","Time":"Time","Timed sessions, review flow, tab locking and completion rules.":"Timed sessions, review flow, tab locking and completion rules.","Top questions for this area":"Top questions for this area","Training":"Training","Training can include classic single-choice questions, multiple-correct questions, free-text questions and PBQs. Multi-select questions need all correct options, free-text questions compare against a model answer, and PBQs use an interactive task component.":"Training can include classic single-choice questions, multiple-correct questions, free-text questions and PBQs. Multi-select questions need all correct options, free-text questions compare against a model answer, and PBQs use an interactive task component.","Training in {course}":"Training in {course}","Training is the low-pressure practice mode. You answer one question at a time, get feedback immediately and can repeat the pool as often as you want. It is best for quick drilling, familiarization and first passes through a topic.":"Training is the low-pressure practice mode. You answer one question at a time, get feedback immediately and can repeat the pool as often as you want. It is best for quick drilling, familiarization and first passes through a topic.","Training mode shows you all questions in the pool. Just start and learn without pressure.":"Training mode shows you all questions in the pool. Just start and learn without pressure.","Training: {pool}":"Training: {pool}","Trouble Spots is the remediation view. It collects questions that currently cause problems, so you can revisit weak points directly instead of running the full queue.":"Trouble Spots is the remediation view. It collects questions that currently cause problems, so you can revisit weak points directly instead of running the full queue.","UI Language affects the app interface labels and controls. Content Language affects the learning material itself, such as translated question text and answers. You can keep the interface in one language and the question content in another.":"UI Language affects the app interface labels and controls. Content Language affects the learning material itself, such as translated question text and answers. You can keep the interface in one language and the question content in another.","Use Training when you want broad, low-pressure practice inside one pool. Use Leitner when you want structured spaced repetition for one pool. Use Smart Queue when you want due questions from several pools in one prioritized review session.":"Use Training when you want broad, low-pressure practice inside one pool. Use Leitner when you want structured spaced repetition for one pool. Use Smart Queue when you want due questions from several pools in one prioritized review session.","User":"User","VirtuProf":"VirtuProf","Wahr/Falsch":"Wahr/Falsch","Wahr/Falsch in {course}":"Wahr/Falsch in {course}","Wahr/Falsch: {pool}":"Wahr/Falsch: {pool}","Welcome back! There are still questions waiting for you in the Leitner system.":"Welcome back! There are still questions waiting for you in the Leitner system.","What are Trouble Spots?":"What are Trouble Spots?","What can I do here?":"What can I do here?","What do I see after Training ends?":"What do I see after Training ends?","What do I see in the exam review?":"What do I see in the exam review?","What do the other personal settings do?":"What do the other personal settings do?","What does Content Language change?":"What does Content Language change?","What does My Progress show?":"What does My Progress show?","What does “Explain this” do?":"What does “Explain this” do?","What does “due” mean in Leitner?":"What does “due” mean in Leitner?","What feedback do I get in Training?":"What feedback do I get in Training?","What happens after a duel ends?":"What happens after a duel ends?","What happens to unfinished league pairings?":"What happens to unfinished league pairings?","What happens when time runs out?":"What happens when time runs out?","What is Calendar Sync for?":"What is Calendar Sync for?","What is Smart Queue?":"What is Smart Queue?","What is Training mode for?":"What is Training mode for?","What is a streak?":"What is a streak?","What is different in Exam mode?":"What is different in Exam mode?","What is the Champions League round?":"What is the Champions League round?","What is the difference between End Exam and Abort?":"What is the difference between End Exam and Abort?","What is the difference between UI Language and Content Language?":"What is the difference between UI Language and Content Language?","What is the difference between a course and a pool?":"What is the difference between a course and a pool?","What is the leaderboard measuring?":"What is the leaderboard measuring?","When does “Open Duel” appear in league play?":"When does “Open Duel” appear in league play?","When should I use Leitner, Smart Queue or Training?":"When should I use Leitner, Smart Queue or Training?","Which question types can appear in Training?":"Which question types can appear in Training?","Who chooses the pool and number of questions?":"Who chooses the pool and number of questions?","Why do I see translated content?":"Why do I see translated content?","Why do I wait for the opponent after answering?":"Why do I wait for the opponent after answering?","Why does a pool show fewer questions than expected?":"Why does a pool show fewer questions than expected?","Why is a pool locked?":"Why is a pool locked?","Why is an exam read-only in another tab?":"Why is an exam read-only in another tab?","Write the admin reply here...":"Write the admin reply here...","Yes. Personal Settings includes a Virtual assistant toggle. If you switch it off, the corner avatar and its automatic hints stop appearing until you enable it again.":"Yes. Personal Settings includes a Virtual assistant toggle. If you switch it off, the corner avatar and its automatic hints stop appearing until you enable it again.","You are inside a true-or-false session. Use it for fast repetition when you want to classify many statements quickly.":"You are inside a true-or-false session. Use it for fast repetition when you want to classify many statements quickly.","You are inside an active Leitner pool. Review the due cards first; new or difficult questions will come back sooner than mastered ones.":"You are inside an active Leitner pool. Review the due cards first; new or difficult questions will come back sooner than mastered ones.","You are inside an active training pool. Start the session to answer mixed questions with direct feedback after every answer.":"You are inside an active training pool. Start the session to answer mixed questions with direct feedback after every answer.","You are inside an exam pool. Work through the whole run first; explanations and correct answers are shown at the end.":"You are inside an exam pool. Work through the whole run first; explanations and correct answers are shown at the end.","You are viewing a regular pool in Leitner mode. Use it to keep difficult questions coming back until they stick.":"You are viewing a regular pool in Leitner mode. Use it to keep difficult questions coming back until they stick.","You are viewing a regular pool in Training mode. This is the fastest way to practice the pool with immediate feedback.":"You are viewing a regular pool in Training mode. This is the fastest way to practice the pool with immediate feedback.","You are viewing a regular pool in exam mode. Treat it like a test run without instant correction.":"You are viewing a regular pool in exam mode. Treat it like a test run without instant correction.","You are viewing a regular pool in true-or-false mode. This is useful for fast recall training.":"You are viewing a regular pool in true-or-false mode. This is useful for fast recall training.","You can keep learning here, and I can explain the most important modes and rules whenever you need a quick reminder.":"You can keep learning here, and I can explain the most important modes and rules whenever you need a quick reminder.","You challenge an opponent from the standings, the opponent accepts it, and the system creates the linked duel. Incoming and outgoing challenges are shown separately so you can see what still needs action.":"You challenge an opponent from the standings, the opponent accepts it, and the system creates the linked duel. Incoming and outgoing challenges are shown separately so you can see what still needs action.","Your message will be stored as a support ticket with context, so an admin can answer it manually later.":"Your message will be stored as a support ticket with context, so an admin can answer it manually later.","Accept":"Accept","Accepted":"Accepted","A classmate challenged you to a duel. Accept it to jump straight into the duel lobby.":"A classmate challenged you to a duel. Accept it to jump straight into the duel lobby.","Cancel invite":"Cancel invite","Canceled":"Canceled","Challenge from {user}":"Challenge from {user}","Challenge opponent":"Challenge opponent","Challenge to {user}":"Challenge to {user}","Challenging...":"Challenging...","Closed":"Closed","Create duel code only":"Create duel code only","Decline":"Decline","Declined":"Declined","Directly challenge an opponent":"Directly challenge an opponent","Duel invites":"Duel invites","Failed to accept duel invite":"Failed to accept duel invite","Failed to cancel duel invite":"Failed to cancel duel invite","Failed to decline duel invite":"Failed to decline duel invite","Failed to load duel invites":"Failed to load duel invites","Incoming duel invites":"Incoming duel invites","Incoming duel invites ({n})":"Incoming duel invites ({n})","Invite accepted. Both players can mark themselves ready now.":"Invite accepted. Both players can mark themselves ready now.","Invite sent. Waiting for the opponent to accept...":"Invite sent. Waiting for the opponent to accept...","Invited":"Invited","No active duel invites right now.":"No active duel invites right now.","No direct opponents are available in this course.":"No direct opponents are available in this course.","Open":"Open","Open duel":"Open duel","Open invites stay here until they are declined, canceled or the duel has been played.":"Open invites stay here until they are declined, canceled or the duel has been played.","Outgoing duel invites":"Outgoing duel invites","Outgoing duel invites ({n})":"Outgoing duel invites ({n})","Pool: {pool}":"Pool: {pool}","Ready":"Ready","The duel invite was canceled.":"The duel invite was canceled.","The duel invite was declined.":"The duel invite was declined.","This duel is ready. Open it from here and play it inside the course duel tab.":"This duel is ready. Open it from here and play it inside the course duel tab.","Your duel invite is waiting for a response from the opponent.":"Your duel invite is waiting for a response from the opponent.","selected pool":"selected pool","this course":"this course","{days} days in a row. Consistency beats intensity.":"{days} days in a row. Consistency beats intensity.","(historisch)":"(historical)","802.1Q":"802.1Q","802.1Q Frame":"802.1Q Frame","Access":"Access","Access VLAN {id}":"Access VLAN {id}","Access-Ports senden untagged, Trunks transportieren mehrere VLANs per 802.1Q.":"Access ports send untagged frames, trunks carry multiple VLANs via 802.1Q.","Adressen":"Addresses","Adresstyp":"Address Type","Aktion":"Action","Alle Aufgaben bearbeitet! {correct} von {total} richtig.":"All exercises completed! {correct} of {total} correct.","Alle Felder":"All Fields","Am Access-Port bleibt der Frame fuer Endgeraete untagged.":"At the access port, the frame remains untagged for end devices.","Anfänger":"Beginner","Anzahl Hosts":"Host Count","Anzahl Subnetze":"Subnet Count","Anzeige-Preset":"Display Preset","Auf dem Trunk wird der 802.1Q-Tag gesetzt; der Native VLAN Traffic kann untagged bleiben.":"On the trunk, the 802.1Q tag is applied; native VLAN traffic may remain untagged.","Ausgangsnetz":"Base Network","Beispiel: 10.0.0.0/24":"Example: 10.0.0.0/24","Beispiel: 192.168.1.0/24 oder 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0":"Example: 192.168.1.0/24 or 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0","Beispiel: 2001:db8::1/48 oder fe80::1/10":"Example: 2001:db8::1/48 or fe80::1/10","Beste Serie: {streak} in Folge":"Best streak: {streak} in a row","Belegte Adressen":"Used Addresses","Benutzerdefiniert":"Custom","Berechnen":"Calculate","Binär-Display":"Binary Display","Bit":"Bit","Bitte ein gültiges Ausgangsnetz fuer den VLSM-Rechner eingeben.":"Please enter a valid base network for the VLSM calculator.","Bitte eine gültige IPv4-Adresse mit Prefix oder Subnetzmaske eingeben.":"Please enter a valid IPv4 address with prefix or subnet mask.","Bitte eine gültige IPv6-Adresse mit Prefix eingeben (z.B. 2001:db8::1/48).":"Please enter a valid IPv6 address with prefix (e.g. 2001:db8::1/48).","Bitte mindestens ein Subnetz mit positivem Hostbedarf angeben.":"Please specify at least one subnet with a positive host requirement.","Broadcast":"Broadcast","CIDR":"CIDR","CIDR-Prefix":"CIDR Prefix","CompTIA Network+ N10-009":"CompTIA Network+ N10-009","Das Ausgangsnetz konnte nicht berechnet werden.":"The base network could not be calculated.","Der Gesamtbedarf passt nicht in den verfuegbaren Adressraum.":"Total demand does not fit in the available address space.","Die Berechnung aktualisiert sich sofort während der Eingabe.":"The calculation updates instantly as you type.","Encapsulation":"Encapsulation","Entfernen":"Remove","Erlaubte VLANs: {ids}":"Allowed VLANs: {ids}","Erklär-Modus":"Explain Mode","Erster Host":"First Host","Falsch":"Wrong","Fortgeschritten":"Advanced","Gateway":"Gateway","Gib oben eine gültige IPv4-Adresse mit Prefix oder Maske ein.":"Enter a valid IPv4 address with prefix or mask above.","Gruppe":"Group","Gruppe {n}":"Group {n}","Gültige Eingabe erkannt.":"Valid input detected.","Host":"Host","Hostanteil":"Host Portion","Hosts":"Hosts","IP/CIDR oder IP + Maske":"IP/CIDR or IP + Mask","IPv6":"IPv6","IPv6-Adresse / Prefix":"IPv6 Address / Prefix","Inter-VLAN-Routing":"Inter-VLAN Routing","Interface":"Interface","Interface-ID":"Interface ID","Ja (RFC1918)":"Yes (RFC1918)","Klasse":"Class","Kompakt":"Compact","Layer-2 Feld":"Layer 2 Field","Leicht":"Easy","Letzter Host":"Last Host","Maximale Server":"Maximum Servers","Mittel":"Medium","Name":"Name","Nein":"No","Netz":"Network","Netz-Bits sind cyan, Host-Bits amber markiert.":"Network bits are cyan, host bits are amber.","Netzadresse":"Network Address","Netzadresse, Broadcast, Binärdarstellung und VLSM direkt im Browser berechnen.":"Calculate network address, broadcast, binary representation and VLSM directly in the browser.","Netzanteil":"Network Portion","Netzanteil: {network} Bits, Hostanteil: {host} Bits":"Network portion: {network} bits, host portion: {host} bits","Netzmaske: {mask}":"Subnet mask: {mask}","Noch {n} Aufgaben":"{n} exercises remaining","Nochmal starten":"Restart","Nur Basics":"Basics Only","Nutzbare Hosts":"Usable Hosts","Nächste Aufgabe":"Next Exercise","Oktett":"Octet","Oktett {n}":"Octet {n}","Passt ins Supernetz":"Fits in Supernet","Pflege VLAN-ID, Name, Subnetz und Gateway fuer dein Segment-Design.":"Manage VLAN ID, name, subnet and gateway for your segment design.","Port-Visualisierung":"Port Visualization","Position":"Position","Prefix":"Prefix","Prefix: {prefix} Bits, Interface-ID: {iid} Bits":"Prefix: {prefix} bits, Interface ID: {iid} bits","Privat":"Private","Prüfen":"Check","Rechenweg":"Calculation Steps","Rechenweg (IPv6)":"Calculation Steps (IPv6)","Rechner":"Calculator","Richtig":"Correct","Richtige Antwort: {answer}":"Correct answer: {answer}","Router-on-a-Stick erstellt fuer jedes VLAN eine Subinterface mit dot1Q-Kapselung.":"Router-on-a-stick creates a subinterface with dot1Q encapsulation for each VLAN.","Routing blockiert":"Routing blocked","Routing moeglich":"Routing possible","Schwer":"Hard","Serie: {streak}":"Streak: {streak}","Subinterface":"Subinterface","Subnetz":"Subnet","Subnetz hinzufügen":"Add Subnet","Subnetzmaske":"Subnet Mask","Subnetzname":"Subnet Name","Subnetzrechner":"Subnet Calculator","Subnetzrechner Tabs":"Subnet Calculator Tabs","Teste dein Wissen mit zufälligen Subnetting-Aufgaben. Du bekommst sofort Feedback zu jeder Antwort.":"Test your knowledge with random subnetting exercises. You get instant feedback on every answer.","Trunk":"Trunk","Ungueltige VLAN-IDs gefunden. Erlaubt sind 1-4094, ausser 1002-1005.":"Invalid VLAN IDs found. Allowed range is 1-4094, except 1002-1005.","VLAN":"VLAN","VLAN {id}":"VLAN {id}","VLAN fuer Vorschau":"VLAN for Preview","VLAN hinzufügen":"Add VLAN","VLAN-ID":"VLAN ID","VLAN-IDs muessen eindeutig sein.":"VLAN IDs must be unique.","VLAN-Tabelle":"VLAN Table","VLSM":"VLSM","VLSM allociert immer größte Netze zuerst und nutzt die Netzadresse des eingegebenen Blocks.":"VLSM always allocates the largest networks first and uses the network address of the given block.","Vergleiche den Ethernet-Frame fuer Access- und Trunk-Ports.":"Compare the Ethernet frame for access and trunk ports.","Verschwendet":"Wasted","Warum?":"Why?","Wildcard":"Wildcard","tagged":"tagged","tagged im Uplink":"tagged in uplink","untagged":"untagged","Übung":"Practice","Übung starten":"Start Practice","{correct} von {total} richtig":"{correct} of {total} correct","When AI is enabled, user questions and the currently displayed quiz question (text, answer options, explanation) are sent to Google Gemini (an external AI service). In exam mode, the correct answer is never transmitted. Error reports stay local and are not sent to Gemini. Admins subject to GDPR/DSGVO must review and accept the":"When AI is enabled, user questions and the currently displayed quiz question (text, answer options, explanation) are sent to Google Gemini (an external AI service). In exam mode, the correct answer is never transmitted. Error reports stay local and are not sent to Gemini. Admins subject to GDPR/DSGVO must review and accept the"}}');

